WEBVTT

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:27.040
Hey, it's me.

00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:36.690
Okay. Okay.

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:41.150
Okay. Okay. Okay. Okay.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:45.820
Logistics screwed up. This is a 12mm flange.

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:47.850
We ordered the 10mm.

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:52.370
We can use it on the Kokuyou, but not Argevollen.

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:54.460
Well, I can see why they'd make that mistake.

00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:56.970
Nothing uses the 10mm.

00:00:56.970 --> 00:00:58.870
Okay, good!

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:03.880
And the captain and Suzushiro-san aren't here to complain for us.

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:06.500
Why were they summoned now, of all times?

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:07.660
I don't know.

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:09.920
Anyway, these flanges...

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:11.800
That's the problem with prototypes.

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:13.950
They're not compatible with anything.

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:16.080
I hear a lot about that,

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:18.120
but are they really that different?

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:20.260
They're not as useful as you'd think.

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:22.230
New one-off prototypes in particular

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:25.760
use far more specialized parts than mass-produced units,

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:28.550
which means you can't use parts from other Trail Kriegers.

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:30.790
I see.

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:34.950
It definitely looks a lot different than the other machines.

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:36.900
Take good care of it,

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:40.710
or you'll be stuck on the sidelines watching when it counts.

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:42.490
I-I'll be careful.

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:44.100
There.

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:46.710
Hey, look at its legs.

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:49.420
The design combines heat radiation with shock absorbers,

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:51.080
which makes it really elegant, don't you think?

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:52.350
Does it?

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:53.720
What are you talking about?

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:56.670
What you need on the battlefield isn't a girl's elegance.

00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:57.930
It's a man's uncouthness.

00:01:57.930 --> 00:02:00.750
The chief is being sexist again.

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:01.880
Yeah.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:02.560
Shut up!

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:05.110
Move your hands, not your mouths.

00:02:05.110 --> 00:02:06.980
So what do we do with the flanges?

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:10.050
Unlike a wife, this thing can't be divorced.

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:12.980
So we'll just have to make it fit.

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:18.870
Someday, in this space deprived of hope,
kono takaki mubou no kuu de itsuka

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:23.540
you'll kneel of your own will.
sono ishi wa hiza wo tateru

00:02:32.590 --> 00:02:34.760
break up foreordination

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:39.640
Was that flame an illusion or a friend?
fake ano hi wa nakama ka

00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:44.350
Am I to venture into the darkness?
susumu beki wa yami ka

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:53.660
You'll find nameless emotions beyond the protruding knife.
knife tsukitateta saki ni shoutai no mienu kanjou

00:02:53.990 --> 00:02:59.490
I can't let this end here yet.
ima wa mada koko de owarenai

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:04.620
I need to get ready to survive.
naraba ikiru junbi wo shiro yo

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:09.920
The passion in my heart only burns hotter.
uzu takaku tsumiageteku netsujou

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:13.430
Needless to say, it burdens me.
omotai ni kimatten darou

00:03:13.430 --> 00:03:14.470
wake up your tough intention
Needless to say, it burdens me.
omotai ni kimatten darou

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:14.880
wake up your tough intention

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:15.840
Go ahead and mock my inexperience on the battlefield.
mijuku da to warau ga ii sa senjou
wake up your tough intention

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:20.100
mijuku da to warau ga ii sa senjou
Go ahead and mock my inexperience on the battlefield.

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:26.730
I'll show you what I've got, bit by bit,
hitotsu zutsu tashikamete yaru kara

00:03:27.190 --> 00:03:28.270
so bring it on.
kakattekoi

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:38.780
break up foreordination

00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:47.440
The blitzkrieg's failure

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:51.520
divided the Ingelmian forces to the north and south.

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:55.510
The Arandas forces had withdrawn once,

00:03:55.510 --> 00:03:58.200
but as the speed of Ingelmia's invasion slowed,

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:02.240
they regrouped and waited for a chance to counterattack.

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:06.040
Small battles broke out all along the front lines,

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:10.160
but some time passed without a large-scale advance.

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:15.490
Independent Unit 8 was deployed all along the battle lines,

00:04:15.490 --> 00:04:19.560
and now they are taking a short rest at Wishpe.

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:57.070
This is paradise.

00:04:58.940 --> 00:05:02.040
That's the first time I've ever heard anyone actually say

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:04.010
"this is paradise" in a hot springs.

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:06.310
I'm old at heart.

00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:11.840
I'm so glad there are hot springs in Wishpe, though.

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:13.130
My skin feels so soft.

00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:14.850
It feels great.

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:20.140
That soft skin is right in front of me...

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:24.260
Try being in my position, with a man's ass in your face the whole time.

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:25.830
I can see them!

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:27.070
Seriously?!

00:05:27.070 --> 00:05:28.690
Where? Where?

00:05:28.690 --> 00:05:30.080
Just kidding.

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:33.270
What the heck? Come on, man!

00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:35.860
Oh, now you've done it!

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:38.440
Come on, try to catch me!

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:39.300
The men's bath is so noisy.

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:40.460
Hold up!
The men's bath is so noisy.

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:40.870
Who's over there?
Hold up!

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:42.090
Who's over there?

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:45.290
There's no way they could see us.

00:05:45.290 --> 00:05:48.620
Why is an idol getting embarrassed over something like this?

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:50.710
You're an idol, Akino-san?

00:05:50.710 --> 00:05:53.420
Just trying to be one. Actually, failed to be one.

00:05:53.420 --> 00:05:54.840
That's so surprising!

00:05:54.840 --> 00:05:57.300
Hey, what kinds of auditions did you do?

00:05:58.980 --> 00:06:00.220
Sing something!

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:09.840
Is this all we need to buy?

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:10.960
Yeah.

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:15.170
Well, if it isn't Okui's boy!

00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:17.810
It's been a long time, gramps.

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:19.530
Oh, you're right.

00:06:19.530 --> 00:06:21.360
It's been quite a while.

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:23.680
Hey, kid, been doing well?

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:24.320
Yeah.

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:26.160
Who is this?

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:28.050
Koshikawa from my squad.

00:06:28.050 --> 00:06:29.520
Nice to meet you.

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:31.210
Is that right?

00:06:31.210 --> 00:06:35.640
You haven't been back here once since you joined the army.

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:38.410
You should show up to the village meetings once in a while.

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:41.040
Yeah, if I have time.

00:06:42.050 --> 00:06:43.900
Ah, how unusual.

00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:45.430
What brings you here?

00:06:45.430 --> 00:06:47.060
Just an errand.

00:06:47.060 --> 00:06:49.230
I can tell you were born in Wishpe.

00:06:49.230 --> 00:06:51.700
It's a simple town with nothing in it.

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:54.140
It'd be more surprising not to run into anybody I knew.

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:55.620
That's nice.

00:06:57.440 --> 00:07:01.630
When I was a kid, I couldn't wait to leave here.

00:07:02.930 --> 00:07:04.080
But it's not bad.

00:07:05.830 --> 00:07:08.820
Ah, pardon me.

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:10.260
Oh, my!

00:07:10.260 --> 00:07:12.500
You're Old Lady Shikinami!

00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:14.650
You haven't kicked the bucket yet?

00:07:14.650 --> 00:07:16.480
I won't die that easy.

00:07:16.480 --> 00:07:19.960
And you didn't get hit by a bullet and blown apart yet?

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:24.580
I won't die before you do, you old hag.

00:07:34.110 --> 00:07:35.600
I'll open your curtains.

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:36.270
Okay.

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:40.870
Man, it's dusty.

00:07:46.760 --> 00:07:48.030
Nobody lives here?

00:07:55.190 --> 00:07:57.120
My parents died a long time ago.

00:07:57.740 --> 00:07:59.240
I just come home once in a while.

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:01.900
I see.

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:08.280
Well, let's get back.

00:08:09.530 --> 00:08:10.800
Sorry.

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:12.180
It's cool.

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:16.720
Okay, turn it on.

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:17.650
Okay!

00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:24.950
It's not perfect,

00:08:24.950 --> 00:08:27.020
but it'll last until our next resupply.

00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:28.090
How's it looking?

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:30.400
Almost there.

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:32.440
Then it's your turn.

00:08:32.440 --> 00:08:34.700
Get the device recognized and linked up.

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:35.690
Okay.

00:08:37.180 --> 00:08:39.170
Hey, why's it all black here?

00:08:40.870 --> 00:08:42.870
That's level two maintenance.

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:44.210
Level two maintenance?

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:47.010
All you can do on-site is level one maintenance.

00:08:47.010 --> 00:08:50.670
You'd have to send it to the factory for anything more.

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:55.100
It's a prototype, so it's filled with Kybernes Manufacturing trade secrets.

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:57.680
We can only do level one maintenance on a few areas of it.

00:08:59.490 --> 00:09:00.940
I knew it.

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:03.720
You went to the hot springs while we were doing maintenance.

00:09:05.650 --> 00:09:07.360
It was great.

00:09:07.360 --> 00:09:09.400
If you want to go to the hot springs, get to work.

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:10.450
Right!

00:09:10.450 --> 00:09:11.820
Hot springs! Hot springs!

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:12.830
Let's finish this up.

00:09:12.830 --> 00:09:14.340
Okay, let's get this done.

00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:14.760
Hot springs! Hot springs!
Okay, let's get this done.

00:09:14.760 --> 00:09:15.790
Hot springs! Hot springs!

00:09:35.640 --> 00:09:37.030
This is Unit 8!

00:09:37.030 --> 00:09:37.890
Yes.

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:43.230
Ingelmia's crossed over Tasca and invaded?

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:47.860
What's the situation?

00:09:47.860 --> 00:09:49.080
Confirming now.

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:50.280
What do we do?

00:09:50.280 --> 00:09:51.530
The captain's not here!

00:09:51.530 --> 00:09:52.490
Be quiet.

00:09:54.580 --> 00:09:57.540
Looks like there's no doubt that Tasca has fallen.

00:09:57.540 --> 00:10:00.570
With Captain Samonji and Sergeant Major Suzushiro absent,

00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:03.170
Sergeant Tanita's in command.

00:10:03.170 --> 00:10:06.290
Sergeant Tanita ate some bad fish and locked himself in the bathroom.

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:07.180
What?!

00:10:07.180 --> 00:10:10.000
He caught a fish from the river and ate sashimi style.

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:11.390
That moron.

00:10:11.390 --> 00:10:14.640
If Sergeant Tanita's out for health reasons, then...

00:10:15.290 --> 00:10:18.890
Me? You want a Trail Krieger pilot taking command?

00:10:18.890 --> 00:10:21.150
I guess she's out.

00:10:21.150 --> 00:10:24.180
That means it's either Okui or Kutsuwada.

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:26.840
Me? No way.

00:10:26.840 --> 00:10:30.400
It'd be better to have someone who knows the local geography.

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:33.290
Knows the local geography?

00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:39.750
Me?

00:10:47.170 --> 00:10:49.710
Okay, hurry up!

00:10:59.140 --> 00:11:02.040
Just buy as much time as you can.

00:11:02.040 --> 00:11:02.800
Roger.

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:04.400
We don't have a lot of items, though.

00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:06.400
Terai! Have we requested reinforcements?

00:11:06.400 --> 00:11:09.400
We have but HQ is hard-pressed to deal with this...

00:11:10.120 --> 00:11:11.330
How many enemies?

00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:13.530
It was a single division that crossed Tasca.

00:11:13.530 --> 00:11:18.190
Looks like a minimum of three battalions are heading here.

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:19.840
What now?

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:23.920
Our highest priority is getting the civilians out of there.

00:11:23.920 --> 00:11:27.060
Once that's done, we counterattack!

00:11:29.480 --> 00:11:31.140
Chief, get ready to drop the bridge.

00:11:31.140 --> 00:11:31.920
Got it!

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:33.550
You heard him.

00:11:33.550 --> 00:11:36.950
You lot ready Argevollen, no matter what.

00:11:36.950 --> 00:11:37.800
Right.

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:43.410
The enemy won't be here for a while.

00:11:43.410 --> 00:11:45.480
You don't need to hurry. There's plenty of time.

00:11:45.480 --> 00:11:47.740
Stay calm as you move.

00:11:47.740 --> 00:11:50.270
I want to die in this town.

00:11:50.270 --> 00:11:54.000
Nobody wants to see you die.

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:55.660
Get the hell out of here.

00:11:56.730 --> 00:11:59.030
I'll keep the town safe.

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:14.920
This is Seeker. The enemy is approaching.

00:12:15.400 --> 00:12:17.400
I'm seeing 12 Trail Kriegers.

00:12:17.400 --> 00:12:18.930
Sending video.

00:12:18.930 --> 00:12:20.500
How's the evacuation coming?

00:12:20.500 --> 00:12:21.810
It's not finished yet.

00:12:21.810 --> 00:12:24.480
The enemy is advancing faster than anticipated.

00:12:24.480 --> 00:12:27.910
At their current rate, they'll soon be within firing range of Wishpe.

00:12:27.910 --> 00:12:29.680
Give me the C10 unit.

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:31.070
Here you go!

00:12:41.080 --> 00:12:43.160
It's quiet.

00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:45.740
The calm before the storm, or whatever?

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:46.910
Shut up.

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:50.070
I can't handle quiet.

00:12:50.070 --> 00:12:53.090
You'll be missing the quiet soon enough.

00:13:35.050 --> 00:13:36.510
It's begun.

00:13:36.510 --> 00:13:40.260
Don't get hit, guys!

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:44.810
I can't belief I ate bad fish at a time like this...

00:13:45.310 --> 00:13:48.640
Don't stop! Head straight for the bridge!

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:50.180
There's plenty of time!

00:13:50.180 --> 00:13:52.690
It's okay! Stay calm and keep going.

00:14:01.940 --> 00:14:03.260
This is Seeker.

00:14:03.260 --> 00:14:04.410
The enemy Trail Kriegers

00:14:04.410 --> 00:14:06.020
have entered the town.

00:14:06.020 --> 00:14:06.770
Roger.

00:14:06.770 --> 00:14:08.160
Everybody, to your stations.

00:14:44.700 --> 00:14:45.480
I got it!

00:14:45.480 --> 00:14:47.540
Okay, head down to the corner of the bakery!

00:14:47.540 --> 00:14:48.580
The bakery?

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:55.210
How's it looking?

00:14:55.210 --> 00:14:57.060
Just a little more! Wrench!

00:14:57.060 --> 00:14:58.380
I'm still using it!

00:14:58.380 --> 00:14:59.050
Jeez!

00:15:01.770 --> 00:15:03.600
There aren't any enemies here.

00:15:05.470 --> 00:15:07.120
Hey, Okui-chan!

00:15:07.120 --> 00:15:09.090
Give me better orders!

00:15:14.060 --> 00:15:16.840
Go right there— I mean, left!

00:15:16.840 --> 00:15:17.780
Which way?

00:15:17.780 --> 00:15:18.840
Left!

00:15:18.840 --> 00:15:22.220
This is Yamanami. How far has the enemy advanced?

00:15:22.220 --> 00:15:25.410
The enemy... The enemy is, um...

00:15:25.410 --> 00:15:26.260
They broke through!

00:15:26.260 --> 00:15:27.870
One Trail Krieger down!

00:15:27.870 --> 00:15:30.100
Huh? Nobody's here to back me up?

00:15:30.100 --> 00:15:31.340
Got a problem!

00:15:31.340 --> 00:15:33.100
Don't everybody talk at once!

00:15:33.100 --> 00:15:35.040
You're the commander right now!

00:15:36.400 --> 00:15:39.840
Captain Samonji does this all the time?

00:15:39.840 --> 00:15:41.770
I'm getting pushed back...

00:15:41.770 --> 00:15:44.260
The enemy's everywhere! What do we do?

00:15:44.260 --> 00:15:45.310
It's me.

00:15:45.310 --> 00:15:47.060
We're almost done evacuating the citizens.

00:15:47.060 --> 00:15:48.360
What's the situation?

00:15:48.360 --> 00:15:50.810
Hurry! The fog's coming soon!

00:15:50.810 --> 00:15:51.770
Fog?

00:15:51.770 --> 00:15:56.270
That's right. There's a thick fog from the river this time of year!

00:15:56.270 --> 00:15:57.980
Fog?

00:15:57.980 --> 00:16:00.270
That's all the reinforcement we need!

00:16:00.270 --> 00:16:01.780
Huh?

00:16:01.780 --> 00:16:03.020
Fog isn't gonna just—

00:16:03.780 --> 00:16:06.740
I guess it did.

00:16:07.970 --> 00:16:09.530
Man, this sucks.

00:16:10.490 --> 00:16:12.120
What is this?

00:16:13.620 --> 00:16:16.320
The fog's great,

00:16:16.320 --> 00:16:18.330
but this is hard to fight in.

00:16:24.090 --> 00:16:25.590
Next...

00:16:31.620 --> 00:16:33.890
It's me. The civilians have all been evacuated.

00:16:33.890 --> 00:16:35.190
Roger.

00:16:35.190 --> 00:16:36.930
The citizens have all crossed the bridge.

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:38.600
Begin our counteroffensive!

00:16:38.600 --> 00:16:40.050
It's too late for that!

00:16:40.050 --> 00:16:41.650
They're too deep within our lines!

00:16:41.650 --> 00:16:43.980
We can't see in this fog, either!

00:16:43.980 --> 00:16:45.900
Sorry, I got here too late.

00:16:47.230 --> 00:16:49.410
Okui! Argevollen isn't out yet!

00:16:50.450 --> 00:16:52.780
The repair isn't done?!

00:16:52.780 --> 00:16:54.580
We might be at our limit...

00:16:54.580 --> 00:16:56.140
That's dangerous!

00:16:56.140 --> 00:16:57.410
The enemy's over here, too!

00:17:12.820 --> 00:17:15.800
I've sighted an enemy rear force of 20 Trail Kriegers.

00:17:19.880 --> 00:17:21.480
Withdraw!

00:17:21.480 --> 00:17:23.540
All forces withdraw!

00:17:25.140 --> 00:17:27.550
Wheel revolution seems stable.

00:17:27.550 --> 00:17:29.160
Oil pressure is stable.

00:17:29.160 --> 00:17:32.910
Subsystem SP readings aren't reaching standard values...

00:17:48.570 --> 00:17:49.930
Is Argevollen ready yet?

00:17:51.380 --> 00:17:52.020
I'm done.

00:17:52.020 --> 00:17:52.950
Same here.

00:17:52.950 --> 00:17:54.560
Okay, Jamie!

00:17:54.560 --> 00:17:55.060
Yeah!

00:17:56.530 --> 00:17:58.420
Argevollen Device Call!

00:17:58.420 --> 00:18:00.490
System bootup sequence start!

